#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-fft-test-flight.rst:7
#: 1654727117e74f1b898a622f7a116fe7
msgid "Initial Flight and Post-Flight Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-fft-test-flight.rst:9
#: ab3d8b9bac4f4b36a160b4b00fba5369
msgid "Perform a hover flight of at least 30s in altitude hold and :ref:`download the dataflash logs <common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-mission-planner>` without the harmonic notch being enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-fft-test-flight.rst:10
#: 47b6f713da1e4674bf66a1aff89cf058
msgid "Graph the log element FTN1.PkAvg which represents the FFT's energy-weighted estimate of the average noise frequency for roll and pitch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-fft-test-flight.rst:12
#: e765156353884a318a451f396546ec45
msgid "On the graph there should be a fairly consistent estimate of the noise peak that corresponds to the motor rotational frequency. On a smaller Copter this is likely to be around 200Hz and on a larger Copter/QuadPlane 100Hz or so. Here is an example from a 5\" quad running on a Pixracer. Once the pilot has throttled up there is a fairly consistent noise level at about 220Hz:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-fft-test-flight.rst:18
#: e8dd6b00c08542da8e03ef40d6a4273c
msgid "If a consistent estimate is obtained, you can then enable the harmonic notch, as described in :ref:`common-imu-fft`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-imu-fft-test-flight.rst:20
#: 4e1b9a63dfc34f43838436d1edd455cf
msgid "In this flight the dynamic harmonic notch was enabled and set to track the FFT determined frequency and FFT analysis of the post-filter log shows that the gyro noise has been effectively eliminated:"
msgstr ""
